Security properties checked:
- Tokens remain behind ITokenStore/SecureStorageService; no preferences persistence or credential logging introduced. Repair warning names only key and error runtime type. No added network transport, dependencies, environment or workflow credentials.
- Required versioned API has no unsafe get/set fallback; custom-store breaking migration explicitly lists the three required members and synchronous shared revision/order requirements. All concrete stores migrated. Revision identity handles ABA, failed attempts, clear and refresh-only writes.
- Certified reads reject mutations issued during reads and pending/bypassed writes/repairs; conditional reservation precedes await. Lost acknowledgements on superseded failed/throwing calls now schedule conservative repair while uncertainty counters remain active. Exhausted repairs read the logical newest state and retain documented process-restart limits.
- Selection guarantees and limits are honest: consumers must compare revision again; conditional applied does not lock an independent rotation through network requests. Existing legacy getAccessToken remains unchanged; parent1196 still requires network adoption. No claim of device-level encryption/platform atomicity verification.

